{"text": "SE,\nSS232 UNIVERSITY OF SOUTH FLORIDA\naNERS TAMPA + ST. PETERSBURG + FORT MYERS + SARASOTA\n\nSune 9, 1981\n\nHonorable Horace R. Kornegay\nPresident\nThe Tobacco Institute, Inc.\n1875 Eye Street, N. W.\nSuite 800\nWashington, D. C, 20006\n\nDear Mr, Kornegay: \\\n\nThis letter is to inform you that as a result of carefully\nevaluating and analyzing the paper by T. Hirayama, entitled\n\"Non-Smoking Wives of Heavy Smokers Have a Higher\u2019 Risk of\nLung Cancer: A Study from Japan,\u201d British Medical Journal,\n282, pages 183-185, January 17, 1981, we reject, as totally\ninconclusive, his finding that non-smoking wives of heavy\nsmokers have a higher risk of lung cancer, We shall attempt\nto briefly summarize some of the important points of our\neyaluation and analysis,\n\nHere we shall consider only a few of the more salient deficiencies\nin the study as published, The first methodological question\nwhich must be considered is the nature of the data ayailable\nto Hirayama, The author presents statistics concerning five\n@iseases, of which only lung cancer shows a significant rela-\ntionship. to the husband's smoking behavior. The author does\nnot indicate how many diseases were considered in all when the\nanalysis was performed. It must be remembered that if, for\ninstance, the incidence of 20 diseases were studied, then the\nodds would fayor finding some significant relationship at the\n5% level even if the husband's smoking was totally unrelated\nto the wife's health, Since significant relationships were not\nfound for other respiratory diseases, such as emphysema, the\npossibility that the conclusion results from this kind of\n\u201cscatter shot\" analysis must be taken seriously.\n\nAnother methodological consideration is the adequacy of the\nsample size for inyestigation of the relevant hypothesis,\nWhile the author emphasizes that 91,540 women co!\nstudy population, lung cancer is, in fact\namong this population and only 174 deaths\noccurred.\n\n(OF SOUTH FLORIDA 1S AN AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EQUAL OFPOATUNITY INSTITUTION\n\nS9IBSHEPZOZ",
